#: api/abilities/settings.php:44
msgid "Describe site"
msgstr ""

#: api/abilities/settings.php:45
msgid "Call this first. Explains how Marketers Delight settings work on this site: active and installed Drop-ins, settings groups and where each can be saved, post types with settings, Collections, and how settings inherit."
msgstr ""

#: api/abilities/settings.php:51
msgid "Describe settings"
msgstr ""

#: api/abilities/settings.php:52
msgid "Lists one settings group's fields: type, label, allowed options, default and limits. Use it before Update settings. A post type group lists the groups it hosts by name; ask for each one with the post type's scope."
msgstr ""

#: api/abilities/settings.php:64
msgid "Get settings"
msgstr ""

#: api/abilities/settings.php:65
msgid "Reads the values saved for a group at a scope, and at each scope it inherits from, nearest first. A value missing from a scope comes from the next one. Use it to find which level sets something before changing it. At post:ID, term:ID or user:ID, leave out group to see everything set on that one item."
msgstr ""

#: api/abilities/settings.php:77
msgid "Update settings"
msgstr ""

#: api/abilities/settings.php:78
msgid "Changes only the values given. null resets a value, so it inherits again. On a checkbox with options, true turns an option on and 0 turns it off over an inherited setting. Colors take a hex, rgba() or palette key; images take { \"id\": attachment ID }. Group and builder items are keyed by ID: a new ID adds an item, null removes one, others stay. Set dry_run to see the changes without saving."
msgstr ""

#: api/abilities/settings.php:86
msgid "The values to change, shaped like the group's fields."
msgstr ""

#: api/abilities/settings.php:90
msgid "A new order for items: the field's name and its item IDs in order, ex: { \"list\": [\"b\", \"a\"] }."
msgstr ""

#: api/abilities/settings.php:101
msgid "Export settings"
msgstr ""

#: api/abilities/settings.php:102
msgid "Returns this site's MD settings as a file Import settings can read, for a backup or another site: design, theme, post type and Drop-in settings, and widgets. Export design alone to share a look. Never includes license or integration keys."
msgstr ""

#: api/abilities/settings.php:109
msgid "Leave out for everything."
msgstr ""

#: api/abilities/settings.php:120
msgid "Import settings"
msgstr ""

#: api/abilities/settings.php:121
msgid "Applies a file from Export settings. Each selected part replaces this site's values, so export a backup first. Set check to see what the file holds and which Drop-ins it needs, without changing anything. Posts, pages and menus aren't in these files."
msgstr ""

#: api/abilities/settings.php:129
msgid "Parts to import, from check. Leave out for all."
msgstr ""

#: api/abilities/settings.php:243
msgid "A value saved at a nearer scope wins: post or term, then taxonomy, then post type. A group lists where it saves in saves_to. Groups without site there have no site-wide value: Layout, Loop and others are set per post type, and post_type:post is the blog. Change something at the level it should apply to, and use null to remove an override."
msgstr ""

#: api/abilities/settings.php:245
msgid "A group's fields can differ by scope: post_fields are what a single post of that type saves, ex: post:ID. Use them instead of writing those details into the content."
msgstr ""

#: api/abilities/settings.php:246
msgid "Brand colors live in colors at site scope, in palette: changing primary there changes everything that uses it."
msgstr ""

